<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Aug numbers in work fall 56,000.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Aug numbers in work fall 56,000.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics</p>
<p>Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN NUMBERS IN WORK		 Aug 96     Jul 96     Aug 95</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(unadj, million)    34.456     34.409     34.797</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(seas adj, million) 34.457     34.513     34.798</p>
<p> Number in work (2)(seas adj, million) 34.505     34.560     34.839</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj,million)	  28.170     28.158     28.471</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)    28.180     28.238     28.482</p>
<p>@ EAST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj, million)	  6.347	6.316	6.380</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)     6.325	6.322	6.357</p>
<p>NOTE - Pan-German figure marked (1) refer to people living in Germany. Those marked (2), as well as all the west and east German figures, refer to people working in the respective regions but not necessarily living in Germany.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
